Forker's note

This is a fork of the original TaylorMade interpreter by Alan Cox. I've
ported it to the Glk api and added support for "Questprobe featuring The
Human Torch and The Thing", graphics and animations, and a couple of beeps
in "Rebel Planet".

The Commodore 64 versions of all the games except "Blizzard Pass" are
supported as well, from .d64 disk images and .t64 tape images.

ZX Spectrum games can be loaded from .sna and .z80 snapshots (48K or 128K)
and from .tap and .tzx tape images, including the tapes that use the
Alkatraz protection. The loading screen of a tape is shown as a title
picture.

"Temple of Terror" comes in three forms: the version with graphics, the
text-only version with longer descriptions from the other side of the tape,
and a combined version with the text of the one and the pictures of the
other. For the Spectrum version, the combined form is offered when the two
sides are separate files in the same folder, with names that differ only in
the last character before the extension: "a" for the graphics side and "b"
for the text-only side (for example "tot-a.tzx" and "tot-b.tzx").

If the picture data of a game cannot be read, the game is played without
graphics.

The following "extra commands" are added to all games, though some games
already had some of them:

#RESTART, #SAVE, #RESTORE, #UNDO, #QUICKSAVE (or #QSAVE), #QUICKLOAD (or
#QLOAD), #TRANSCRIPT ON and #TRANSCRIPT OFF (or #SCRIPT ON and #SCRIPT OFF).

They also work without the "#". LOAD means the same as RESTORE, OOPS and BOM
the same as UNDO, and RAMSAVE, RAMLOAD, RAM SAVE and RAM RESTORE the same as
QUICKSAVE and QUICKLOAD.

The original README below is kept as Alan Cox wrote it. Where it disagrees
with this note (graphics, supported games, how to run the interpreter), this
note is the one that is up to date.

-- Petter Sjölund, May 2023, updated October 2026


Original README:


	TaylorMade v0.4		(c) 2004 - 2016 Alan Cox
				All Rights Reserved
				See COPYING for more information

Introduction

	Taylormade is a basic text only engine for running the later
	Adventure International UK authored games. This is not the
	same as SAGA+ although some games were recoded from SAGA+.

	Taylormade knows how to parse Spectrum .sna snapshot files
	containing these games and uses patterns in the game binary
	to locate table pointers. Currently the code will load most
	but not all the games in this format.

	To run use "taylormade game.sna".


Features

	Taylormade should eventually support all the games in this
	format. There are several complications to this goal. The
	first is that the game engine changes features by release
	much more than the Scott Adams engine did. 

	The game supports the basic commands found in all the games
	and the extensions that are so far analysed and identified.

	Graphics are not currently supported.

Working Games

	Rebel Planet

	Blizzard Pass

	He-man
		Has RAM save/load features (supported). Appears to
	have an interpreter "GET ALL" that is not.

	Temple Of Terror
		Much like He-man in game features but also adds
	an "oops" function to go back one move. The oops function 
	is supported.

	Kayleth
		Pulls some tables wrongly from the .sna but close

Untested

	Torch & Thing

